  'A Gothic Revival brick farmhouse of 1877, two and a half stories, T-shaped, five bays wide in front, with an enclosed one-story portico at the centre door; Wikipedia names Ernest Hoffman as its architect. A barn and a shed went with it on the National Register in 1985.',
