  'A "pattern book" cottage of 1874 designed by William M. Woollett, an L-shaped two-story house in the Picturesque Cottage manner, with diamond-shaped windows in its gable ends and a jerkin-head roof on the wing. A garage and a well house were listed with it on the National Register in 1985.',
